.TH "RAPTOR-TABLES" 1 "2026-10" "RAPTOR Studio" "RAPTOR Studio Manual"
.SH NAME
raptor\-tables \- export input and result tables
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBraptor tables\fR [\-h] [\-\-run] [\-\-drivers] [\-\-capacity\-rule {proportional,marginal,first_failed}] [\-\-table KEY] [\-\-list] [\-\-format {csv,txt,report,xlsx,ods}] [\-o DIR] [\-\-find TEXT] [\-\-replace TEXT] [\-\-column COLUMN] [\-\-whole] [\-\-case\-sensitive] [\-\-in\-place] [\-n N] [\-t T] [\-\-stop KIND[=VALUE]] [\-\-stats\-start T] [\-\-seed N|new] [\-\-block\-streams {model,separate}] [\-j N] [\-\-timeout DURATION] [\-\-analysis LIST] [\-\-precision P] [\-\-precision\-metric NAME] [\-\-min\-trials N] [\-\-max\-trials N] [\-\-precision\-batch N] [\-\-precision\-confidence C] [\-\-importance MODE] [\-\-weak\-type TYPE] [\-s PATH=VALUE] [\-\-set\-file FILE] [\-\-save\-model PATH] MODEL
.SH DESCRIPTION
Write the model's input tables (and, with \-\-run, the result tables of a fresh run) as CSV, text or a spreadsheet.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Options
.TP
\fB\-\-run\fR
run the model first and include result tables
.TP
\fB\-\-drivers\fR
with \-\-run: also work out what caused each outage and who lost the capacity, adding the downtime\-driver, lost\-capacity and year\-by\-year tables (needs the model's event log recording)
.TP
\fB\-\-capacity\-rule\fR \fI{proportional|marginal|first_failed}\fR
with \-\-drivers: how lost flow is shared among the elements down at once (default proportional, which sums to the engine's own lost flow)
.TP
\fB\-\-table\fR \fIKEY\fR
a table key (see \-\-list); repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-list\fR
list the available tables and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI{csv|txt|report|xlsx|ods}\fR
output format(s); default csv
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIDIR\fR
folder (default ./Tables beside the model)
.TP
\fB\-\-find\fR \fITEXT\fR
with \-\-column/\-\-replace: change matching cells instead of exporting
.TP
\fB\-\-replace\fR \fITEXT\fR
replacement text for \-\-find
.TP
\fB\-\-column\fR \fICOLUMN\fR
file column name or index for \-\-find
.TP
\fB\-\-whole\fR
match the whole cell, not a substring
.TP
\fB\-\-case\-sensitive\fR
match case (default insensitive)
.TP
\fB\-\-in\-place\fR
write replacements back to MODEL
.SS Run control
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-runs\fR \fIN\fR
number of runs (default: the model's)
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-length\fR \fIT\fR
run length for a time\-terminated run
.TP
\fB\-\-stop\fR \fIKIND[=VALUE]\fR
time | failures=N | cycles=N (default: the model's)
.TP
\fB\-\-stats\-start\fR \fIT\fR
start statistics at T
.TP
\fB\-\-seed\fR \fIN|new\fR
salt every random stream: a number repeats a run (a GUI run's seed with \-j 1 for Cores 1, \-j 2 for more); 'new' draws one and reports it (default: the model's saved seed, else Raptor's fixed table)
.TP
\fB\-\-block\-streams\fR \fI{model|separate}\fR
separate: every block that shares a random stream gets its own for this run, as the GUI's Run panel Streams option (the model file is not changed); model: the blocks' own (default: the model's saved choice)
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-jobs\fR \fIN\fR
parallel workers (default 1; N>1 is reproducible but not draw\-identical to 1)
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fIDURATION\fR
give up after DURATION, e.g. 90s, 10m (default 10m); partial results are kept
.TP
\fB\-\-analysis\fR \fILIST\fR
weak,cost,capacity (replaces the model's setting); 'none' clears all
.TP
\fB\-\-precision\fR \fIP\fR
run until the watched metric's relative half\-width is P, e.g. 10%% or 0.1 (implies growing batches; ignores \-\-runs)
.TP
\fB\-\-precision\-metric\fR \fINAME\fR
metric watched by \-\-precision (default system.ao; a probability is watched as 1 \- value, a time as itself)
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-trials\fR \fIN\fR
first \-\-precision batch (default 50)
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-trials\fR \fIN\fR
most \-\-precision may run (default 20000)
.TP
\fB\-\-precision\-batch\fR \fIN\fR
smallest \-\-precision step (default 50)
.TP
\fB\-\-precision\-confidence\fR \fIC\fR
confidence of the \-\-precision interval (default 0.95)
.TP
\fB\-\-importance\fR \fIMODE\fR
IEC 61078 Annex D importance measures estimated by re\-simulation: improvement (RRW, Vesely\-Fussell), risk (RAW), both (adds Birnbaum). Costs one extra batch per block, two for 'both'
.TP
\fB\-\-weak\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR
weak\-link analysis type
.SS Changing parameters (a copy; the model file is untouched unless \-\-save\-model)
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-set\fR \fIPATH=VALUE\fR
change one field, repeatable; see 'raptor help set\-paths'
.TP
\fB\-\-set\-file\fR \fIFILE\fR
many PATH=VALUE lines (or a TOML/JSON table)
.TP
\fB\-\-save\-model\fR \fIPATH\fR
also write the changed model to PATH
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBraptor\fR(1)
